$post_body = <<<'HTML'
<p>Roller shades generally suit a kitchen or bathroom window better than Roman shades because flat, moisture-resistant fabric holds up to steam, splashes, and grease more easily than the soft folds of a Roman shade. Roman shades still work well in a bathroom or kitchen that gets light daily use, especially away from the sink or stove, and many homeowners choose them for the softer look they bring to the room. Deciding between Roman shades or roller shades usually comes down to how much daily moisture a specific window actually sees. Both the <a href="%BASE%/window-treatments/shades/roman-shades/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Roman shades</a> and roller shades lines at Creative Blinds and Drapes come in moisture-resistant fabric options suited to these rooms.</p>
%IMAGE1%
<h2 id="why-moisture-and-grease-change-the-calculation">Why Moisture and Grease Change the Calculation</h2>
<p>Kitchens and bathrooms create conditions other rooms do not, and every fabric offered by <a href="%BASE%/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Creative Blinds and Drapes</a> is chosen with this in mind:</p>
<ul class="bp-list">
  <li>Steam from cooking or showering can settle into fabric folds and lead to mildew over time if a shade is not moisture-resistant.</li>
  <li>Grease near a stove clings to fabric texture more than a flat, smooth surface.</li>
  <li>Flat roller shade fabric wipes clean in seconds, while a folded Roman shade takes more care to clean properly.</li>
  <li>Vinyl or faux-wood blinds are sometimes chosen instead of either fabric option for a sink window that gets heavy daily use.</li>
</ul>
<h2 id="when-a-roman-shade-still-makes-sense-in-these-rooms">When a Roman Shade Still Makes Sense in These Rooms</h2>
<p><strong>A Roman shade is not ruled out everywhere in a kitchen or bathroom.</strong></p>
<ul class="bp-list">
  <li>A window over a bathtub, away from direct splash, can handle a Roman shade without trouble.</li>
  <li>A kitchen window over a sink that sees light, everyday use instead of heavy daily cooking works fine with the right fabric.</li>
  <li>Roman shades bring a softer, more finished look that some homeowners prefer over a flat roller shade in a small powder room.</li>
  <li>A moisture-resistant or laminated Roman shade fabric closes much of the performance gap with <a href="%BASE%/window-treatments/shades/roller-shades/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">roller shades</a>.</li>
</ul>
<h2 id="does-window-placement-change-the-recommendation">Does Window Placement Change the Recommendation?</h2>
<p><strong>Where the window sits in the room matters as much as the room type itself.</strong></p>
<ul class="bp-list">
  <li>A window directly above a sink or stove favors a roller shade for easy cleaning.</li>
  <li>A window on a side wall, away from water and heat, gives a Roman shade more room to work well.</li>
  <li>Large windows in an open kitchen benefit from the lower cost of roller shades across multiple openings.</li>
  <li>A single accent window in a bathroom is often where homeowners choose the softer Roman shade look.</li>
</ul>
%IMAGE2%
<h2 id="roman-shades-vs-roller-shades-for-wet-rooms">Roman Shades vs Roller Shades for Wet Rooms</h2>
<div class="compare-table-wrap">
<table class="compare-table">
  <thead><tr><th>Factor</th><th>Roman Shades</th><th>Roller Shades</th></tr></thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr><td>Moisture resistance</td><td>Good with treated fabric</td><td>Very good, flat and wipeable</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Grease resistance</td><td>Fair</td><td>Strong</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Look</td><td>Soft, finished folds</td><td>Clean, flat</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Best placement</td><td>Bathtub windows, light-use kitchens</td><td>Sink windows, stovetop-adjacent windows</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Cleaning</td><td>More involved</td><td>Quick wipe-down</td></tr>
  </tbody>
</table>
</div>
<p>For a window that sees heavy steam or splashing, roller shades are the safer pick, while Roman shades fit well in lighter-use kitchen and bathroom windows where the softer look matters more. Anyone unsure which fits their specific window can <a href="%BASE%/contact/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">schedule a free in-home consultation</a> to see fabric samples up close. Our guide on <a href="%BASE%/blog/what-window-shades-are-in-style-in-2026/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">which window shade styles are popular in 2026</a> covers how both options are trending in kitchens and bathrooms this year.</p>
HTML;

